WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.167
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.167
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.567
You're here. You made it.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:08.200
Thank you for watching at home.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.934
Well, guys,
today, President Biden

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:13.267
received a briefing on
the upcoming hurricane season

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:16.467
and talked about what the U.S.
is doing to prepare for it.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.267
Yep. Biden was like,
"Are you reading the news?

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.968
My whole presidency
has been hurricane season."

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.267
But Biden's confident
the U.S. will be prepared.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:27.067
He said, "I'll know when
the big hurricane is coming

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.300
when my right knee
starts aching."

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.334
Ooh! Yeah, you feel it.
Something's coming.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.567
Meanwhile, last night,

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:39.834
Pennsylvania held its
Senate primary elections.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:42.968
And while Dr. Oz is in the lead
for the Republican nomination,

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:44.767
more votes have to be counted

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.834
because the race
is still too close to call.

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.234
But this is kind of great.

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.634
I mean, for once, it's nice
to have a doctor waiting for us.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.033
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:57.868
"We're not ready yet. Almost."

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.434
Yeah, as of right now,
Dr. Oz is in first place,

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.300
David McCormick is in second,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.067
and the "Cash Me Outside" girl
is in third.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.701
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.133
-Former president Trump
endorsed Dr. Oz

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:12.434
and he thinks Dr. Oz
should just declare victory now.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.200
Dr. Oz was like,
"Donald, I think you're

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.968
suffering from
premature election."

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.467
-Hey!

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:21.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:24.601 --> 00:01:26.200
Election.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.667
-If Dr. Oz does win,
he'll go on to face the winner

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:32.467
of last night's Democratic
primary, John Fetterman.

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:33.934
Can we see what that matchup
would look like?

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:37.767
Yeah. It's a
morning-talk-show host

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.868
against a morning-talk-show
host's security guard.

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:43.200
Let's get to some fun news.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.000
I want to say congrats to
the class of 2022,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.534
because it's
officially graduation season.

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:48.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:50.601
Congratulations. You did it.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.067
Yeah.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:58.133
Saw the kids out on the street
today looking good.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.868
Congrats.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.367
And get this.

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:03.734
Today, Taylor Swift delivered
the NYU commencement address

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:04.868
at Yankee Stadium.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.567
Yeah. Of course,
the ceremony lasted a while,

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:14.767
because Taylor did the speech
once, then had to re-record it.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.367
But it's commencement season,
which is when famous speakers

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:18.834
give helpful advice
to graduates.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:21.367
So, with that in mind,
here with some sound advice

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:23.601
is our sound engineer,
Steve Mandel.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:24.701
Steve?

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:28.100
-Always give like
30% effort at work.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:32.033
That way, when you give 50%,
they'll be like, "Wow.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.000
He's really working hard."

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.601
-[ Whispering ]
Sound advice from Steve Mandel.

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:38.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.601
That's nice.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:43.934
It's good to see Steve.
-Great advice.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:45.033
-You guys see this?

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:47.300
Australian Prime Minister
Scott Morrison

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.667
is out on the campaign trail,
alright?

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.534
And today, he played soccer
with some young kids.

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:54.000
Yeah, let's see how that went.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.968
Yep. Oh!

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:02.534
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:03.868
That's amazing.

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:05.601
It took himself, the kid,
and his campaign down under.

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:07.434
It's interesting.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.601
Well, guys, we have Tim McGraw
here on the show tonight.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
The one and only.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.167
Yep, he stars in the

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:21.067
"Yellowstone"
spin-off series "1883."

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.400
And now I saw that
Helen Mirren and Harrison Ford

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.767
are starring in another

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:27.534
"Yellowstone" spin-off
called "1932."

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:31.968
Yep, "1932" will focus on
the pandemic, historic drought,

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:35.033
and the depression,
or, as everyone in 2022 put it,

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.000
"Gee, what's that like?"

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:38.934
Some more entertainment news.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:41.267
The game show
"Wheel of Fortune" is going on

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.300
its first-ever live tour.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.667
And we actually got a
sneak peek of the first episode.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:46.734
Take a look at this.

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:50.834
-Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.601
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:58.834
-What?
-It looks intense.

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:00.567
-Yeah. Wow!

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.667
-How about some more advice
from Steve Mandel?

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:03.667
Steve, anything?

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:07.400
-Find a need, fill a need.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.300
For example,
I sell urine to guys on parole.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.534
-[ Whispering ]
Sound advice from Steve Mandel.

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:18.434
[ Cymbal crash ]
-Find a need and fill a need.

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:20.501
-Wow!

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:23.267
-Hey, guys,
this has been going viral.

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:26.000
The world's most
inconvenient convenience store

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.400
hangs off a cliff in China
and sells snacks to climbers.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.300
Look at this. Check this out.
Look at this. Crazy.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.667
-Oh!
-Yeah. And this is annoying.

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:37.634
It's cash only,
but there's an ATM 5 miles up.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.334
-Oh.

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:41.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.334
And, finally, is time for our
latest installment of

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.501
"Tonight Show Polls."

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:50.901
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

